{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"BGN-PCGN:urd-Arab:Latn:2007","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"bgnpcgn","id":"2007","language":"iso-639-2:urd","source_script":"Arab","destination_script":"Latn","name":"Romanization of Urdu (2007)","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/693788/ROMANIZATION_OF_URDU.pdf","creation_date":"2007","confirmation_date":"2017-11","description":"The following is the approved romanization system for\n    deriving standard spellings of Urdu geographical names for\n    Pakistan. It was jointly adopted by BGN and PCGN at the\n    23rd BGN/PCGN Conference in Washington, DC, in 2007 and it\n    is based on the Hunterian romanization system for Urdu,\n    which has been used by the Surveys of India and Pakistan\n    for romanizing Urdu geographical names for more than one\n    hundred years. The BGN/PCGN system laid out below includes\n    diacritical marks in order that the original script can be\n    derived from the romanized form (i.e. it is reversible).\n    For desk users requiring a diacritic-free form, these\n    diacritics can simply be removed. In every case the same\n    basic Roman-script characters are kept as are used in the\n    Hunterian system. The BGN/PCGN forms have further been\n    designed to harmonize with the BGN/PCGN Persian\n    romanization system.","notes":["1. When the vowel sign zīr ( ِ) occurs word-finally in the\n first element of a compound, it is assumed to mark the\n Persian izafat\n morpheme, and is romanized -e, not i.","2. The source of almost all example names is the 1951\n Census of Pakistan, Village List, Northwest Frontier\n Province, Chitral\n State. Office of the Provincial Superintendant of Census,\n North-West Frontier Province, Peshawar.","3. No examples of aspirated dental r (rh, رھ ( were found,\n though this phoneme is assumed to be part of the phonology\n of\n Urdu, and was therefore left out of Table 2.","4. Note that the short vowels in the Urdu examples are not\n pointed.","5. Occasionally, sequences of /z/ or /s/ plus /h/ may be\n encountered, i.e. z·h, s·h. These may be romanized with the\n Unicode\n 'center dot' (U+00B7) separating the two letters, to\n distinguish them from the digraphs /zh/ and /sh/.","Commented tests are blocked by this issue https://github.com/interscript/interscript/issues/572\n depends on the different ways of handling ي to y or e AND و to u or o"]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"parallel","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"alias","name":"space"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":""},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"آبَاد"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ﷲ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Allāh"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"َ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"a"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"َ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":""},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"ة"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"َ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":""},"after":{"kind":"group","items":[{"kind":"string","value":"a"},{"kind":"any","of":[{"kind":"string","value":"h"},{"kind":"string","value":"|"},{"kind":"string","value":"t"}]}]}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ْ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":""}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ٙ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ê"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"group","items":[{"kind":"string","value":"ِ"},{"kind":"any","of":[{"kind":"string","value":"ي"},{"kind":"string","value":"|"},{"kind":"string","value":"ی"}]}]},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ī"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ِ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"i"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ے"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"e"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"آ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ā"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"َا"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ā"}},{"kind":"sub","fr